{
 "scope": "An auditable SUB-BLOCK of the codimension-m regular coarea case: the fibre Jacobian identity matching the ambient coarea density with the graph area density of B2, in linear and C1 form, plus the measure-preserving orthogonal splitting. NO COAREA FORMULA IS PROVED. No hole migrated. The log-concave Cheeger-Buser line belongs to collaborator Wang Haocheng and was not touched.",
 "head": "34b92695ece4f636a1a7f1eafbbf41c685ee0348",
 "origin_main": "34b92695ece4f636a1a7f1eafbbf41c685ee0348",
 "incoming_receipt": "build/verification/20260916T150413.981186Z/report.json",
 "incoming_snapshot": "95ebf9f762031e9b1d6eb46b0d239bc4ea979b0c3d8a8fc7ef87cfe18a8ea756",
 "incoming_entries": 537,
 "incoming_replayed_modules": 206,
 "round_decision": {
  "question": "route decomposition or a direct proof of the codimension-m regular case",
  "answer": "neither in full: deliver one complete, auditable sub-block and state the rest exactly",
  "reason": "the scalar L9 chain has four stages; stages 1 and 2 alone are ImplicitGraph (859 lines) plus RegularChart (164) plus SubgraphDivergence (859), and the codimension-m analogue needs a PARAMETRIC implicit function theorem into an m-dimensional target and an m-dimensional fibrewise change of variables. Neither fits in one round. Stage 4, the pointwise density matching, is the only genuinely new mathematics that is independent of the charting machinery, so it and the linear/measure backbone of stage 2 were finished instead of leaving half a chain."
 },
 "new_declarations": [
  "Analysis.det_id_add_comp_comm",
  "Analysis.normDet_adjoint",
  "Analysis.coareaJacobian_eq_normDet",
  "Analysis.IsVectorGraphSplitting",
  "Analysis.graphProj_adjoint",
  "Analysis.IsVectorGraphSplitting.perp (prime)",
  "Analysis.IsVectorGraphSplitting.proj_left",
  "Analysis.IsVectorGraphSplitting.proj_right",
  "Analysis.IsVectorGraphSplitting.norm_add_sq",
  "Analysis.IsVectorGraphSplitting.comp_adjoint",
  "Analysis.isVectorGraphSplitting_orthogonal",
  "Analysis.finrank_orthogonal_ker_eq",
  "Analysis.splitVectorIsometry",
  "Analysis.splitVectorIsometry_apply",
  "Analysis.measurePreserving_split",
  "Analysis.coareaJacobian_eq_normDet_mul_normDet_graphMapLinear",
  "Analysis.normDet_fderiv_mul_coareaJacobian",
  "Analysis.graphMapLinear_eq_graphLinear",
  "Analysis.normDet_graphMapLinear_eq_graphJacobian",
  "Analysis.abs_deriv_mul_norm_gradient_of_vectorGraphSplitting",
  "CoareaGraphJacobianAudit.route_A0_false (route statement A0 disproved)"
 ],
 "new_mathematics": {
  "weinstein_aronszajn_linear_map_form": "det (1 + X comp Y) = det (1 + Y comp X) for X : H -> W and Y : W -> H, the two identity maps living on DIFFERENT spaces. Mathlib has the matrix statement only (Matrix.det_one_add_mul_comm). This is exactly the passage from the Gram determinant on the target (a coarea Jacobian) to the Gram determinant on the parameter space (an area Jacobian).",
  "linear_identity": "coareaJacobian L = normDet (L comp kappa) * normDet (graphMapLinear iota kappa A), under an orthogonal splitting, the codimension match finrank K = finrank W, and the slope equation (L comp kappa) comp A = -(L comp iota) which says the graph lies in ker L",
  "C1_identity": "normDet (D_t psi) * coareaJacobian (fderiv u x) = normDet (graphMapLinear iota kappa (D_y psi)) along a C1 level family u (iota y + kappa (psi (y,t))) = t; implicit differentiation supplies both the slope equation and (L comp kappa) comp D_t psi = 1",
  "measure_backbone": "(y,z) |-> iota y + kappa z is Lebesgue measure preserving from H x K onto V, via the L2 product and a linear isometric equivalence; no residual constant"
 },
 "hypotheses": "only differentiability of u at the point for the C1 form; the level family is allowed on the whole space in the audit. NO finiteness, boundedness, integrability, regular-value or SFinite hypothesis anywhere.",
 "codimension_hypothesis": {
  "statement": "finrank K = finrank W",
  "necessary": true,
  "how_shown": "not asserted but exhibited: CoareaGraphJacobianAudit.fails_without_codimension proves that with finrank W < finrank K and L surjective the right-hand side is 0 (the normal volume factor is rank deficient) while the left-hand side is not; CoareaGraphJacobianAudit.necessity instantiates it with the zero subspace of R^2 as parameter space, its orthogonal complement (the whole plane) as normal factor and R as target, where orthogonality, spanning and the slope equation all hold"
 },
 "scalar_consistency": {
  "density": "Analysis.coareaJacobian_fderiv already identifies the ambient density with the gradient norm for W = R",
  "volume_factor": "Analysis.normDet_graphMapLinear_eq_graphJacobian identifies the new graph volume factor with the proved graphJacobian for a one-dimensional normal factor",
  "identity": "Analysis.abs_deriv_mul_norm_gradient_of_vectorGraphSplitting: for m = 1 the new C1 identity is literally the scalar abs_deriv_mul_norm_gradient"
 },
 "is_not": [
  "no coarea formula of any codimension is proved",
  "the codimension-m regular case is NOT completed",
  "no parametric implicit-function charting in codimension m",
  "no fibrewise m-dimensional change of variables",
  "no local-to-global patching and no weighted slice measurability in codimension m",
  "nothing about the critical set, sharp finite-regularity Sard, the two Cheeger comparisons or the five Energy holes"
 ],
 "remaining_work_for_the_regular_case": [
  "codimension-m local graph family from a parametric implicit function theorem (scalar analogues: exists_regularChart, levelChart_inverse)",
  "m-dimensional fibrewise change of variables on the image of t |-> psi (y,t), on the Tonelli backbone measurePreserving_split proved this round",
  "assemble with normDet_fderiv_mul_coareaJacobian and the proved B2 hausdorffNormalized_image_vectorGraphMap into a local coarea equality",
  "countable cover and disjoint patching, plus codimension-m weighted slice measurability (scalar analogue OpenSliceMeasurable.lean)"
 ],
